Z||000004||frontal lobe||11-08-2000||12:16 AM||||I played 18 holes of golf once with former NBA player Paul Mokeski.<P>I shook hands once with Dean Smith, coach of North Carolina.  He was very gracious, even though he meets about 10 million people.<P>I stood shoulder to shoulder with Ted Kennedy at a stop light in Washington, DC., and I did NOT heckle him.<P>Wisconsin senator Herb Kohl and former Marquette coach Al McGuire stopped at our table in a Denny's and rubbed my 10 month old daughter's baby head.  I guess you do stuff like that if you are a politician.||||reg||1
